{"type":"standard","title":"Shiinoki Cultural Complex","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Shiinoki Cultural Complex</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q11585956","titles":{"canonical":"Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex","normalized":"Shiinoki Cultural Complex","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Shiinoki Cultural Complex</span></span>"},"pageid":79314109,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Shiinoki_Geihinkan.jpg/330px-Shiinoki_Geihinkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":248},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/Shiinoki_Geihinkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1600,"height":1200},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1336515738","tid":"a6c55991-0192-11f1-9674-f5dc8cc94a66","timestamp":"2026-02-04T06:28:00Z","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Shiinoki_Cultural_Complex"}},"extract":"Shiinoki Cultural Complex is in Kanazawa, Japan. It is housed in the former Ishikawa Prefectural Government Building, which was completed in 1924 and designed by architect Kenkichi Yabashi (1869–1927). It is located at 920-0962 Ishikawa, Kanazawa, Hirosaka, 2 Chome−1−1 on the south side of Kanazawa Castle Park.","extract_html":"<p><b>Shiinoki Cultural Complex</b> is in Kanazawa, Japan. It is housed in the former Ishikawa Prefectural Government Building, which was completed in 1924 and designed by architect Kenkichi Yabashi (1869–1927). It is located at 920-0962 Ishikawa, Kanazawa, Hirosaka, 2 Chome−1−1 on the south side of Kanazawa Castle Park.</p>"}